::ingredients

(garlic, large) 4-8 cloves
(spring onion) as needed
(cardamom seeds) ~10
(star anise) 4-5
(ginger) as needed
(cinnamon) 3-5 sticks
(beef, diced) 300g
(beef marrow bones) 3
(beef bouillon) 1-3 cubes
(coriander) to taste
(lime) 1, to taste
(sauce choice) = (fish sauce) to taste -OR- (oyster sauce) to taste
(sweetener) = (honey) to taste -OR- (brown sugar) to taste
(rice noodles) as needed
(water) as needed

::equipment

(oven)
(tray)
(pot)
(tea strainer, optional)

::instructions

(oven) <heat, temperature not stated>
(garlic) + (cardamom seeds) + (cinnamon) + (star anise) + (ginger) <toast, oven tray, until browned>
(beef marrow bones) + (water) <boil> <skim, remove most scum>
    + {toasted spices} <add, optionally in tea strainer>
    + (beef bouillon) + (beef) + (sauce choice) + (sweetener) <simmer, covered, couple of hours>
(rice noodles) <cook, few minutes, al dente>
{spices} <remove, from broth>
(coriander) + (spring onion) <chop>
<serve, noodles and broth contents in bowls, garnish with coriander and spring onion>
# Lime is listed but not explicitly assigned a method step.

::story

Vietnamese Pho Soup is a tea-like, beef based soup with a flavor profile that differentiates it from the traditional Western palette. This recipe is designed to be as easy to make as possible, while simultaneously being as based as possible.

